romanized:
Uhé tré na dippan baldī aggé—
Pavvas dhāṛ té āvé aggé;
Laggas dukkh té ghar ā̃ haggé;
Mard na hōvis ghar, te khāvé aggé.

literal_en:
The same three things should not be thrown into flaming fire—
The herdsman if robbers have fallen on him and he come away;
The man who has been attacked by illness and defiles the house;
The woman if her husband be not at home and she eat first.
